<title>UK: TABLE-Pearson 96 profit hit by charge.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Pearson 96 profit hit by charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, total)     42.9		   vs  47.1</p>
<p> Shr pence (pre-excep)  30.6		   vs  28.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 11.1		   vs  10.175</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 18		     vs  16.5</p>
<p> Pre-tax		    356.8		  vs 365.1</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-excep	251.8		  vs 235.7</p>
<p> Op profit (pre charge) 281.3		  vs 259.6</p>
<p> Turnover		  2186		    vs1830.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax, pre-exceptional profits in a range between 226 and 290 million stg.</p>
<p>The extraordinary items include a 231.3 million stg profit on the sale of local newspaper group Westminster Press and a 100 million stg charge for improper accounting at Penguin USA.</p>
<p>Full company name - Pearson Plc.</p>
</text>
